<title>USA: Dow says to repurchase 20 mln common shrs.</title>
<headline>Dow says to repurchase 20 mln common shrs.</headline>
<dateline>MIDLAND, Mich. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dow Chemical Co said its board of directors approved a new stock buy-back program authorizing repurchase of an additional 20 million shares.</p>
<p>The new program will begin once the current repurchase authorization is completed during the second quarter of 1997, Dow said.  The shares will be bought on the open market or in private transactions, it said.</p>
<p>Since January 1995, Dow has repurchased 55.3 million shares of its own stock, equivalent to about 20 percent of its outstanding stock.  As of April 30, Dow had 231.9 million shares outstanding, it said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
